-NOT SHIPPED (design was completed and verified but abandoned per the scope decision above, recorded here in case Chorus survives past TAT-70's rewrite and this resurfaces):
-- Real fix: a viewport-relative render budget, gated on `tui.mode === 'fullscreen'` and re-evaluated at every render() call (0.84.0 made fullscreen runtime-toggleable via /settings, so mode cannot be cached at widget-registration time).
-- Height signal: `tui.terminal.rows`, read fresh each render via a narrow `{ mode, terminal: { rows } }` viewport type threaded into ChorusRoomTranscript's constructor (TUI structurally satisfies this).
-- Budget rationale (upgraded from an arbitrary fraction): dock (widget + editor minSize 3 + footer 1 + status) must stay under terminalRows-1, since crossing that line collapses the transcript in one step rather than degrading gracefully. A budget of ~1/3 of terminal rows for the widget satisfies that constraint from very short terminals upward.
-- Two independent caps, named to prevent re-merging: CHORUS_TRANSCRIPT_ENTRY_LIMIT stays a DATA RETENTION bound (what the broker/render considers as candidate entries); a separate RENDER bound (the line budget) truncates further only in fullscreen mode.
-- Truncation: drop oldest entries first, guarantee at least the most recent entry renders (further line-truncated if needed), show a "+N earlier" indicator with its own line self-accounted against the budget (never additive) - except at the degenerate 1-row-budget floor, where the indicator is dropped rather than exceeding budget.
-- Regular mode: must not regress - no new bound imposed, since it has no bound today and none is needed (see mechanism trace above).
